    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_paired_split_biform_offline_norm_factorization",
    "title": "A=1 quadratic paired split-biform off-line norm factorization",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "classified-row locator power and bounded residual norm",
    "statement": "For each live A=1 quadratic pair-boundary split biform, the product over every off-line supported parameter fiber is divisible by the classified-row locator to the full parameter-row degree. The quotient has an exact degree cap and loses exactly the sum of all fiber X-degree drops. In the extremal profile the cap is 3e-9 or 2e-7 according to d_A, equals the complete triple-union, padding, and exceptional-row slack, contains every selected padded-heavy root, and is uniquely reconstructed from explicit classified-row tangent products. The strict profile obeys the analogous printed quadratic ledger.",
